2. DATA PRODUCED BY THIS WORK -- Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Applies to the outputs of the analysis: the thirteen production sensitivity
grids and the two auxiliary curves in constraint_boundaries/, the calibration
and expected-band outputs in constraint_boundaries/toys/, MANIFEST.tsv,
README.md and this file.

You are free to share and adapt this material for any purpose, including
commercially, provided you give appropriate credit, link to the licence, and
indicate if changes were made. Full terms:

    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

Cite as the paper above, together with this deposit's DOI.


3. THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL -- NOT ours to license
-----------------------------------------------

Two sets of files in this deposit are derived from other people's published
work. Neither the MIT grant of section 1 nor the CC-BY grant of section 2
extends to them, and nothing here licenses their reuse.

(a) constraints_data/*/*.txt -- 53 curves digitised by us from figures published
    by other groups (Arina et al. 2021; Ibarra et al. 2024; Hambye et al. 2021;
    XENONnT 2023; LZ 2022; Fortin & Tait 2012; the Fermi-LAT and H.E.S.S. line
    searches; CTA and XLZD projections). The underlying limits are the property
    of their authors and publishers. The digitisation is ours, and carries our
    reading error rather than theirs. constraints_data/PROVENANCE.tsv gives the
    source paper, arXiv identifier and source figure for each file.

    If you use one of these curves, cite the source paper, not this deposit. If
    you redistribute one, satisfy yourself that the source permits it. They are
    included here only so that the paper's figures can be redrawn exactly, which
    is what the paper's Data Availability statement promises.

(b) data/slatyer2016_feff_3keV.dat and data/slatyer2016_feff_PPPC_3keV.dat --
    energy-deposition efficiency tables from Slatyer (2016), included under the
    same reasoning and subject to that work's own terms.

The per-bin posterior chains that drive the halo bounds are NOT in this deposit.
They belong to the companion paper (arXiv:2607.08552) and are available with
that work, under whatever terms it sets.
